<http://data.silknow.org/object/a530b115-89a5-3df6-8089-f8ff19eafc3d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Buddhist priest's robe (<i>kesa</i>) of brocaded silk. The garment is made up from three and a half widths of silk. It has a pattern of colourful (red, pink, violet and green) flowers and butterflies in 1/2 twill on a gold 2/1 twill ground. Details are marked in gilt paper strips. The garment is divided by couched cord into a border and many rectangular compartments. There are patches of similar tissue with a salmon ground sewn onto the two lower corners (those in the upper corners have disappeared). The <i>kesa</i> is lined with three and a half widths of white silk with a 5/1 twill pattern of floral scrolls on a 2/1 twill ground. There is an interlining of white paper."@en , "Kesa (Buddhist priest's mantle), of brocaded silk, Japan, 18th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/26ee7789-607a-3e9d-909b-d8ccb2ac044b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Kesa (Buddhist priest's mantle), of brocaded silk, Japan, 18th century"@en , "Buddhist priest's robe (<i>kesa</i>) of brocaded silk. The garment is made up from three and a half widths of silk. It has a pattern of colourful (red, pink, violet and green) flowers and butterflies in 1/2 twill on a gold 2/1 twill ground. Details are marked in gilt paper strips. The garment is divided by couched cord into a border and many rectangular compartments. There are patches of similar tissue with a salmon ground sewn onto the two lower corners (those in the upper corners have disappeared). The <i>kesa</i> is lined with three and a half widths of white silk with a 5/1 twill pattern of floral scrolls on a 2/1 twill ground. There is an interlining of white paper."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/a530b115-89a5-3df6-8089-f8ff19eafc3d/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/a530b115-89a5-3df6-8089-f8ff19eafc3d/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.1-1951" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O491627> .

